1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,654
Voucher registration: ask AI in plain
language to read scanned invoice PDFs,

2
00:00:05,654 --> 00:00:09,998
fill them into Excel, and then turn the
whole workflow into a skill.

3
00:00:09,998 --> 00:00:14,150
This demo is for administrative staff, and
no coding is required.

4
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:17,924
The data are five scanned expenditure
vouchers.

5
00:00:17,924 --> 00:00:20,447
The top half is the voucher mounting form;

6
00:00:20,447 --> 00:00:23,511
the bottom half has an invoice or receipt
attached.

7
00:00:23,511 --> 00:00:27,656
These are scans with no text layer, so the
AI has to read the images.

8
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:32,583
The file to fill is record.xlsx, copied
from a template.

9
00:00:32,583 --> 00:00:38,060
Its columns are account code, control
number, invoice number, invoice amount,

10
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:43,607
total amount, vendor tax ID, buyer title,
liability account, and project code.

11
00:00:44,567 --> 00:00:47,367
The approach: let the AI look first, then
act.

12
00:00:47,367 --> 00:00:49,984
Agree on the rules, do one record to
check,

13
00:00:49,984 --> 00:00:53,514
and finally package the workflow that
worked into a skill.

14
00:00:54,467 --> 00:00:58,302
Step one, ask first: "Take a look at what
the Excel file needs.

15
00:00:58,302 --> 00:01:00,676
Can those fields be found in the PDFs?"

16
00:01:00,676 --> 00:01:03,476
The AI finds that the PDFs have no text
layer,

17
00:01:03,476 --> 00:01:06,520
so it converts each page to an image and
reads it.

18
00:01:07,467 --> 00:01:08,886
From the sample row,

19
00:01:08,886 --> 00:01:14,349
the AI also infers that the vendor tax ID
is not NCHC's own number, 80778299;

20
00:01:14,349 --> 00:01:16,194
it should be the seller's.

21
00:01:16,194 --> 00:01:21,374
It flags issues on its own, too: 340 is a
receipt with no invoice number,

22
00:01:21,374 --> 00:01:26,908
331 has a different project code, and the
liability account isn't on the PDFs.

23
00:01:27,867 --> 00:01:31,540
Step two, agree on highlighting rules:
yellow for anything missing,

24
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:35,049
blue for anything uncertain, plus a cell
comment explaining why.

25
00:01:35,049 --> 00:01:38,174
A color legend goes in the top-right
corner of the sheet,

26
00:01:38,174 --> 00:01:40,586
so anyone who opens the file understands
it.

27
00:01:41,533 --> 00:01:45,447
Step three, do one first: "Just do the
first one;

28
00:01:45,447 --> 00:01:48,243
I want to check that it's correct."

29
00:01:48,243 --> 00:01:51,918
Uncertain cells get a blue fill and a
comment.

30
00:01:51,918 --> 00:01:57,270
For example, the invoice amount is the
tax-included total, 262,688;

31
00:01:57,270 --> 00:01:59,746
before tax it would be 250,179.

32
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:03,049
Step four: once that checks out,

33
00:02:03,049 --> 00:02:07,601
fill in the other four and explain every
yellow and blue cell.

34
00:02:07,601 --> 00:02:12,888
The five records total 488,548, and the
total row becomes a SUM formula.

35
00:02:12,888 --> 00:02:17,293
The invoice number for receipt 340 is left
blank, in yellow.

36
00:02:18,233 --> 00:02:21,452
Step five is the key: turn the workflow
into a skill.

37
00:02:21,452 --> 00:02:24,853
Everything we confirmed lives only in this
conversation;

38
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:27,039
start a new chat and it's forgotten.

39
00:02:27,039 --> 00:02:30,137
A skill is a work manual that saves this
knowledge.

40
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:32,575
How do you make a skill?

41
00:02:32,575 --> 00:02:37,125
No coding: just ask the AI in natural
language, the way you normally talk.

42
00:02:37,125 --> 00:02:40,506
"Package the procedure we confirmed today
into a skill,

43
00:02:40,506 --> 00:02:44,318
including where to read each field, the
yellow and blue rules,

44
00:02:44,318 --> 00:02:48,560
and how to cross-check the amounts." The
AI creates voucher-to-excel.

45
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:52,248
SKILL.md is the work manual, with the
workflow, field rules,

46
00:02:52,248 --> 00:02:53,662
and highlighting rules.

47
00:02:53,662 --> 00:02:57,781
The scripts folder holds code that writes
to Excel, applies colors,

48
00:02:57,781 --> 00:03:01,040
and computes totals, with the same result
every time.

49
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:06,356
Later, in a new chat, just say: "I've
added three new invoices;

50
00:03:06,356 --> 00:03:11,680
please enter these records into Excel."
The AI finds the skill automatically.

51
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:15,137
Before reusing it, check which agent
you're using:

52
00:03:15,137 --> 00:03:20,875
Claude reads .claude/skills in the project
folder; other agents use .agents/skills.

53
00:03:21,833 --> 00:03:26,812
Bonus demo: two AI agents working
together, one doing and one reviewing.

54
00:03:26,812 --> 00:03:31,168
First, Gemini copies the template, reads
the five invoice PDFs,

55
00:03:31,168 --> 00:03:32,897
and fills in record.xlsx.

56
00:03:32,897 --> 00:03:37,807
It finds the voucher-to-excel skill we
just made and follows its rules.

57
00:03:38,767 --> 00:03:42,490
Gemini fills in all five: a total of
488,548,

58
00:03:42,490 --> 00:03:48,115
and receipt 340 has no invoice number, so
it's left blank in yellow.

59
00:03:48,115 --> 00:03:49,687
It all looks right.

60
00:03:49,687 --> 00:03:51,094
But is it really?

61
00:03:52,033 --> 00:03:54,463
Now Claude takes the reviewer's role:

62
00:03:54,463 --> 00:03:59,913
"Please cross-check the PDFs against the
Excel sheet and verify that it's correct."

63
00:03:59,913 --> 00:04:04,575
Claude converts each PDF to images and
checks invoice numbers, amounts,

64
00:04:04,575 --> 00:04:06,085
and tax IDs row by row.

65
00:04:06,085 --> 00:04:09,894
The verdict: all five are correct, with
nothing to change.

66
00:04:09,894 --> 00:04:14,556
It also notes that some tax IDs are stored
as text and some as numbers,

67
00:04:14,556 --> 00:04:16,132
and suggests one format.

68
00:04:17,067 --> 00:04:18,425
One does, one reviews:

69
00:04:18,425 --> 00:04:23,177
a second agent cross-checking is like
colleagues reviewing each other's work,

70
00:04:23,177 --> 00:04:25,152
so mistakes are easier to catch.

71
00:04:25,152 --> 00:04:28,176
And the same skill works across different
agents.

72
00:04:29,133 --> 00:04:32,951
To recap: let the AI understand first,
then agree on rules.

73
00:04:32,951 --> 00:04:36,123
Do one record, confirm it, then process
the rest.

74
00:04:36,123 --> 00:04:38,905
Turn the workflow that worked into a
skill,

75
00:04:38,905 --> 00:04:41,624
and keep refining it through conversation.

